  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "Two hands 又 joined, representing friendship; 又 also provides the pronunciation"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of two hands togther to convey the meaning \"friend\"."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "同𢖽爲友。从二又。相交友也。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Phono-semantic compound (形聲 /形声, OC *ɢʷɯʔ): phonetic 又 (OC *ɢʷɯs) + phonetic 又 (OC *ɢʷɯs)\nShuowen: two hands, therefore friendship.\nEndoactive derivation of 右 (OC *ɢʷɯʔ, “right”) (Schuessler, 2007).\nTraditionally considered cognate with Tibetan གྲོགས (grogs, “friend; companion”) (STEDT). Schuessler rejects this comparison, believing that the -r- is the initial of a root instead of the g-, and thus that any Chinese cognate of the Tibetan word must also have an initial *r (which 友 does not have)."
    }
  ],
